            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of pyometra manifesting as an acute abdomen: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>200-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0049475515587167</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous perforation of pyometra is a rare entity with a reported incidence in the range of 0.01-0.05%. The clinical picture is similar to peritonitis arising from intestinal perforation and commonly the correct diagnosis is only made perioperatively. We report a case in an elderly postmenopausal woman presenting with an acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
